## Results

Both runs started Linux `/init`, reached `retired=2,999,999,998`, stopped at
`budget_exhausted`, and passed exact nonce validation. Series scenario outcome
was `passed`; the strict comparator returned `matches=false`, exit code 1, with
unexplained `machine_observations` and `ordered_uart_bytes` differences.

| Run | RDTSC reads by CPL `[0,1,2,3]` | PIT `0x61` | PIT `0x42` | PM reads | #PF / #GP(0) | Halt idle ns | Virtual ns | Residual ns | IRQ0 edges / delivered | Quanta |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 0001 | `[34422255, 0, 0, 0]` | 1 | 16,672 | 230 | 35 / 1 | 1,560,610 | 37,440,718,608 | 34,438,928,000 | 34,783 / 34,788 | 34,548,755 |
| 0002 | `[34461280, 0, 0, 0]` | 1 | 16,672 | 230 | 33 / 1 | 1,452,243 | 37,479,635,241 | 34,477,953,000 | 34,822 / 34,827 | 34,587,024 |

Residual is `virtual_ns - retired - halt_idle_ns - pm_timer_reads × 1,000 ns`.
Each residual exactly equals `(rdtsc_reads + pit_0x61_reads +
pit_0x42_reads) × 1,000 ns`. All counted RDTSC reads occurred at CPL0; the CPL1,
CPL2 and CPL3 buckets were zero in both runs. The 39,025-read CPL0 difference
accounts arithmetically for the 39,025,000 ns residual difference. This
localizes the variation to kernel-mode execution but does not identify its
callsite or cause. Full `virtual_ns` differs by 38,916,633 ns because run 0002
also spent 108,367 ns less in explicit halt idle.

The recorded CPL3 retired count was 1,093 in each run; the nine-entry syscall
journal (8 returns) was identical. Delivered exceptions differed: 35 `#PF` +
1 `#GP(0)` versus 33 `#PF` + 1 `#GP(0)`. `cr3_changes` was 26,618 in both and
the final set detail was `Run(InstructionBudgetExhausted)` in both. IRQ0 edges
and deliveries differed by 39; quanta differed by 38,269.

Both UART transcripts printed the `Run /init as init process` line before the
nonce. They still differ in strict ordering: the `audit: type=2000` line occurs
before five `thermal_sys: Registered thermal governor` lines in run 0001 and
after them in run 0002. Their terminal panic snapshots also contain different
optional stack frames: run 0001 includes `schedule`, `do_nanosleep`,
`tty_ldisc_deref`, `hrtimer_nanosleep` and other frames; run 0002's varying
frames include `irqentry_exit` and `exc_page_fault`. The current panic
normalizer rejects unknown optional frames rather than dropping them. These
observations do not establish benignity or a root cause. S5-07 remains
blocked/unaccepted; do not normalize them without further evidence.

